Reading this as: redesign of an existing listening product for design-conscious
music listeners, with an Epidemic Sound editorial liner-notes language,
leaning toward Inter + Newsreader italic, paper white, and oxblood chapters
instead of hot pink.

Dials: DESIGN_VARIANCE 6 / MOTION_INTENSITY 3 / VISUAL_DENSITY 3.

Before changing UI, read `src/app/theme.css`, `src/app/variables.css`, and
`src/app/tokens.json`.

Hard rules from the Jadid / Epidemic Sound spec:
- Canvas is Paper White `#ffffff`. Warm surface is Bone `#f1f0eb`.
- Oxblood `#4a242c` substitutes Hot Pink. Use it as a full-bleed chapter, never
  as a small tint, never as the filled CTA.
- The only filled button is Ink Black `#000000` with white type, 0px radius.
  Ghost buttons are Bone with black type. No shadows.
- 0px radius on cards, buttons, inputs, images. Badges may be 9999px.
- Inter for all functional UI. Newsreader (sebentaFont substitute) for display
  only. Emphasis inside headlines is italic of the same serif, never a color swap.
- Photographs arrive at full fidelity. No duotone, no overlay labels on images.
- Page max-width 1200px. Section gap 64px. Card padding 24px.
- Chromatic cadence: mostly white/bone, then one oxblood block, then charcoal
  if needed. Never stack two chromatic sections.
- Brand stays Resonant. No skip / next control.
- Homepage still names Listen Now, Favorite Songs, Connect Apple Music.
- Every Noise atlas is navigation only. Never write a genre field onto stored
  catalog records.
- No em-dash in visible copy.
